Package: SpaCoDA
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Transcriptomics Deconvolution and Niche Discovery (Paper
        Methods)
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Kai", email = "hsiaokaifan@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: The methods of the accompanying paper. Estimates spot-level
    cell-type proportions from spatial transcriptomics by a variance-weighted,
    platform-corrected non-negative least-squares fit against a single-cell
    reference, with an optional graph-Laplacian spatial smoothness term (off by
    default); the hot loop is implemented in 'RcppArmadillo'. Finds spatial
    niches per section from the Aitchison distance between spot compositions
    fused with the spatial distance, integrates them across sections into
    meta-niches, tests whether the composition is spatially organised, and
    provides 'Seurat' wrappers.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: Matrix, nnls, FNN, Rcpp, igraph (>= 1.3.0), irlba, stats,
        methods
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: Seurat, SeuratObject, harmony, RSpectra, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
